WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.080
welcome back to the David Pakman show.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.080
Okay.

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:05.890
Yet as it sometimes happens on the show, we
will have problems with last minute guests,

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:09.320
cancellations and today was one of those days.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:13.900
So in order to not delay production of the
show, which would be hugely disrespectful

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.400
to our audience, we're going to take a few
phone calls.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.180
There were a lot of people who want to get
on today and see what is on people's minds.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:23.180
Of course the phone number is always (617)
830-4750.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:29.070
Let's go first to our caller from the five
to zero area code five two zero.

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:31.250
What's your name and where are you calling
from today?

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:33.640
Hey, what's up David?

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:36.020
Uh, this is Justin calling from Albuquerque.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.040
Hey Justin, what's going on?

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:45.750
Hey, uh, I was just wondering your opinion
on, uh, people who become sort of apolitical

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.880
for one reason or another.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:56.460
Um, like I've met quite a few people who like
sort of fell for the Donald Trump, uh, rhetoric

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:02.530
and they just like the side that politics
is evil in general.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:03.530
Hmm.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.550
So do you think that it would be worth trying
to talk those people back into politics?

00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:12.080
Well, so when you say that it fell for the,
for Trump, did they vote for Trump and then

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.130
after voting for him, say they're no longer
engaging in public politics?

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.780
What do you mean?

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:23.960
Yeah, I mean in, uh, I mean anecdotally, but
in several cases of people I've met, they

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.800
voted for Trump or they just decided that
Trump and Hillary were equivalent.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:34.460
Um, and I could see how they came to that
conclusion cause when I was younger I could

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.310
maybe fall for that kind of mindset.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:42.020
Um, but I was just wondering if you thought
it would be worth trying to talk them into

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:45.590
politics or if they would maybe fall for the
same sort of rhetoric.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:49.400
Well, here's the thing, here's what I think
is important to explain to those folks in

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:51.729
the same way that not voting is not a neutral
act.

00:01:51.729 --> 00:01:56.030
When you don't vote, that is a proactive decision
you make not to participate.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:58.280
And it does tend to help Republicans.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.871
So if you're saying, I'm just not going to
vote and I'm, I'm staying out of it, you're

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:06.760
actually typically helping the more conservative
candidate in most places who often is a Republican

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:11.020
and in primaries you end up helping often
the most extreme republican in the same way

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.780
you can opt out of participating in the electoral
process.

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.140
You can't really opt out of politics.

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:21.981
I mean, if you don't live in the middle of
nowhere, uh, in, in a completely, you know,

00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:25.880
disconnected way in some kind of state of
nature in rural northern Alaska or something

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.880
like that.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.720
And even then, this may not even apply.

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.740
You are subject to what is going on politically.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:35.740
If you're in touch with the financial system,
if you have a job, if you earn money, if you

00:02:35.740 --> 00:02:42.760
have a house, whatever you are involved in
politics, you might be choosing not to participate

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:43.760
ELAC.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:44.760
Totally.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.010
But I think the point I would make to people
when they say I'm just not involved in politics

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.090
is you're involved in politics.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:53.240
You're just choosing not to try to influence
what that looks like.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.360
But either way you're involved in effected
by it.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:56.360
That that's the reality.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.880
You can't really not be.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.599
Yeah, I mean that's, that's a great point.

00:03:02.599 --> 00:03:10.320
But um, like you think that people kind of
avoid politics for like emotional reasons

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.320
or,

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.320
sure.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.320
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.320
I mean, listen, it's exhausting.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:18.880
It's exhausting and particularly now it's
extremely depressing and you know from the

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.220
time I'm done with the Friday show until the
weekend ends and I'd start preparing the Monday

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:27.940
show, I pay attention to no news and politics
and its particular, yeah,

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:28.940
I understand Stan,

00:03:28.940 --> 00:03:34.270
the instinct, I just think it all ultimately
comes down to you're effected by, by politics,

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.690
no matter whether you participate, not, and
it's a question of do you want to have a say

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.690
or don't you?

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:43.440
But either way you are going to suffer from
the repercussions of the decisions made by

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:45.340
those who are participating.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:52.870
And if I could quickly ask a follow up, like
if someone, if you get the sense that someone

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:58.650
is avoiding politics for those emotional reasons,
do you think that it would be bad to try to

00:03:58.650 --> 00:03:59.650
talk them into this?

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:05.129
Because from my perspective, things have just
gotten so intense that like, it's like you

00:04:05.129 --> 00:04:07.020
said, you just, you have to be involved.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:10.180
Yeah, I mean, listen, I would be empathetic.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.180
I would say empathy.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.180
I would be empathetic.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.730
I would say I understand that.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:19.220
What I would encourage them to consider is
that the short term increased involvement,

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:25.759
if we all did it might give a significant
longer term, uh, circumstance significantly

00:04:25.759 --> 00:04:29.389
better, longer term sort of circumstances
during which we can focus on other areas of

00:04:29.389 --> 00:04:33.050
our lives without having to be so worried
about what it is that's going on in Washington.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:34.340
That that's the argument I would make.

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.490
Justin, thank you.

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:36.650
I really appreciate the call.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.400
I've got a bunch of people holding, so I'm
going to let you go, but I do hope to hear

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.240
from you again.

